        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-25\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML file syntax using Bun's built-in YAML parsing capabilities. The command accepts one or more file paths as arguments, validates each file, and reports results with appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        A[yaml-validator.ts<br/>Entry Point]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Core Layer\"]\n        B[validator.ts<br/>Validation Logic]\n        C[formatter.ts<br/>Output Formatting]\n    end\n\n    subgraph External[\"External\"]\n        D[(File System)]\n        E[js-yaml<br/>Bun Built-in]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    A --> C\n    B --> D\n    B --> E\n    C --> F[stdout/stderr]\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Structure\n\nThe implementation follows the existing project structure with modular separation of concerns:\n\n```\nsrc/\n  yaml-validator/\n    index.ts        # CLI entry point\n    validator.ts    # Core validation logic\n    formatter.ts    # Output formatting utilities\n    types.ts        # TypeScript type definitions\n    validator.test.ts  # Unit tests\n```\n\n### 2.2 Data Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as yaml-validator/index.ts\n    participant Val as validator.ts\n    participant Fmt as formatter.ts\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant YAML as js-yaml\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate file1.yaml file2.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse argv for file paths\n\n    loop For each file path\n        CLI->>Val: validateFile(path)\n        Val->>FS: Bun.file(path).text()\n        alt File not found/readable\n            FS-->>Val: Error\n            Val-->>CLI: FileAccessError\n        else File readable\n            FS-->>Val: content\n            Val->>YAML: parse(content)\n            alt Parse error\n                YAML-->>Val: YAMLException\n                Val-->>CLI: ValidationError\n            else Parse success\n                YAML-->>Val: parsed object\n                Val-->>CLI: ValidationSuccess\n            end\n        end\n        CLI->>Fmt: formatResult(result)\n        Fmt-->>CLI: formatted message\n        CLI->>User: stdout/stderr output\n    end\n\n    CLI->>Fmt: formatSummary(results)\n    Fmt-->>CLI: summary message\n    CLI->>User: Summary to stderr\n    CLI->>User: Exit with code (0/1/2)\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Type Definitions\n\n```typescript\n// types.ts\n\n/** Result of validating a single file */\nexport type ValidationResult =\n  | { status: 'success'; filePath: string }\n  | { status: 'validation_error'; filePath: string; error: YAMLError }\n  | { status: 'file_error'; filePath: string; error: FileError };\n\n/** YAML parsing error details */\nexport interface YAMLError {\n  message: string;\n  line?: number;\n  column?: number;\n}\n\n/** File access error details */\nexport interface FileError {\n  code: string;  // 'ENOENT', 'EACCES', etc.\n  message: string;\n}\n\n/** Aggregate results for multiple files */\nexport interface ValidationSummary {\n  total: number;\n  passed: number;\n  failed: number;\n  fileErrors: number;\n}\n\n/** Exit codes */\nexport const ExitCode = {\n  SUCCESS: 0,\n  VALIDATION_ERROR: 1,\n  FILE_ERROR: 2,\n} as const;\n\nexport type ExitCode = typeof ExitCode[keyof typeof ExitCode];\n```\n\n### 3.2 Validator Module\n\n```typescript\n// validator.ts\n\nimport { load } from \"js-yaml\";\nimport type { ValidationResult, YAMLError, FileError } from \"./types\";\n\n/**\n * Validate YAML syntax for a single file.\n *\n * @param filePath - Absolute or relative path to YAML file\n * @returns ValidationResult indicating success or type of failure\n */\nexport async function validateFile(filePath: string): Promise<ValidationResult> {\n  // 1. Attempt to read file\n  // 2. Attempt to parse YAML\n  // 3. Return appropriate result type\n}\n\n/**\n * Validate multiple YAML files.\n *\n * @param filePaths - Array of file paths to validate\n * @returns Array of ValidationResult for each file\n */\nexport async function validateFiles(filePaths: string[]): Promise<ValidationResult[]> {\n  // Process all files, collecting results\n  // Never short-circuit on errors\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 Formatter Module\n\n```typescript\n// formatter.ts\n\nimport type { ValidationResult, ValidationSummary } from \"./types\";\n\n/**\n * Format a success message for stdout.\n *\n * @param filePath - Path to the validated file\n * @returns Formatted success message\n */\nexport function formatSuccess(filePath: string): string {\n  return `${filePath}: valid`;\n}\n\n/**\n * Format a validation error message for stderr.\n *\n * @param filePath - Path to the invalid file\n * @param error - YAML parsing error details\n * @returns Formatted error message\n */\nexport function formatValidationError(filePath: string, error: YAMLError): string {\n  const location = error.line ? ` (line ${error.line})` : '';\n  return `${filePath}${location}: ${error.message}`;\n}\n\n/**\n * Format a file access error message for stderr.\n *\n * @param filePath - Path that could not be accessed\n * @param error - File system error details\n * @returns Formatted error message\n */\nexport function formatFileError(filePath: string, error: FileError): string {\n  return `${filePath}: ${error.message}`;\n}\n\n/**\n * Format aggregate summary for stderr.\n *\n * @param summary - Aggregated validation results\n * @returns Formatted summary message\n */\nexport function formatSummary(summary: ValidationSummary): string {\n  // Format: \"Validated N files: X passed, Y failed, Z file errors\"\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 CLI Entry Point\n\n```typescript\n// index.ts\n\nimport { validateFiles } from \"./validator\";\nimport { formatSuccess, formatValidationError, formatFileError, formatSummary } from \"./formatter\";\nimport { ExitCode } from \"./types\";\n\nasync function main(): Promise<never> {\n  const filePaths = process.argv.slice(2);\n\n  if (filePaths.length === 0) {\n    console.error(\"Usage: bun run validate <file1.yaml> [file2.yaml] ...\");\n    process.exit(ExitCode.FILE_ERROR);\n  }\n\n  const results = await validateFiles(filePaths);\n\n  let hasFileError = false;\n  let hasValidationError = false;\n\n  for (const result of results) {\n    switch (result.status) {\n      case 'success':\n        console.log(formatSuccess(result.filePath));\n        break;\n      case 'validation_error':\n        console.error(formatValidationError(result.filePath, result.error));\n        hasValidationError = true;\n        break;\n      case 'file_error':\n        console.error(formatFileError(result.filePath, result.error));\n        hasFileError = true;\n        break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Print summary if multiple files\n  if (results.length > 1) {\n    const summary = calculateSummary(results);\n    console.error(formatSummary(summary));\n  }\n\n  // Exit code priority: file error > validation error > success\n  if (hasFileError) {\n    process.exit(ExitCode.FILE_ERROR);\n  } else if (hasValidationError) {\n    process.exit(ExitCode.VALIDATION_ERROR);\n  } else {\n    process.exit(ExitCode.SUCCESS);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n```\n\n### 3.5 Data Model\n\nNo persistent data storage. The command processes files and produces output in a single invocation.\n\n**In-Memory Data Structures:**\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph Input\n        A[string[]: filePaths]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Processing\n        B[ValidationResult[]]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Output\n        C[stdout: success messages]\n        D[stderr: error messages + summary]\n        E[exit code: 0/1/2]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    B --> C\n    B --> D\n    B --> E\n```\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Justification |\n|-------|------------|---------------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |\n| YAML Parser | js-yaml (Bun built-in) | No new dependencies required |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() API | Native Bun file handling |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing project test framework |\n\n**Critical Constraint**: No new dependencies. The implementation uses only:\n- Bun runtime built-ins\n- @types/bun (existing devDependency)\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| Task | Component | Description | Effort |\n|------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| T1 | types.ts | Define TypeScript interfaces and types | Small |\n| T2 | validator.ts | Core validation logic using js-yaml | Medium |\n| T3 | formatter.ts | Output formatting utilities | Small |\n| T4 | index.ts | CLI entry point with argument parsing | Small |\n| T5 | package.json | Add \"validate\" script | Trivial |\n| T6 | validator.test.ts | Unit tests for validator and formatter | Medium |\n\n**Estimated Total Effort**: Small-Medium (single session)\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Types have no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Validator and formatter only depend on types\n3. [T4, T5] - CLI and package.json script depend on core modules\n4. [T6] - Tests depend on all implementation components\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (validator uses types)\n- T3 -> T1 (formatter uses types)\n- T4 -> [T1, T2, T3] (CLI integrates all modules)\n- T5 -> T4 (script references entry point)\n- T6 -> [T1, T2, T3, T4] (tests verify all components)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4 -> T6\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Type | Value | Rationale |\n|-----------|-------|-----------|\n| Valid YAML parsing | HIGH | Core app functionality |\n| Invalid YAML detection | HIGH | Core app functionality |\n| File not found handling | HIGH | Exit code correctness for CI/CD |\n| Permission denied handling | MEDIUM | Error handling path |\n| Exit code verification | HIGH | CI/CD integration correctness |\n| Output stream routing | HIGH | stdout vs stderr correctness |\n| Summary formatting | LOW | Cosmetic, not critical path |\n\n### 7.2 Test Cases\n\n```typescript\n// validator.test.ts\n\ndescribe(\"validateFile\", () => {\n  test(\"returns success for valid YAML\", async () => {\n    // Create temp file with valid YAML\n    // Validate and expect success status\n  });\n\n  test(\"returns validation_error for invalid YAML\", async () => {\n    // Create temp file with invalid YAML\n    // Validate and expect validation_error status with line number\n  });\n\n  test(\"returns file_error for non-existent file\", async () => {\n    // Attempt to validate non-existent path\n    // Expect file_error status with ENOENT\n  });\n\n  test(\"includes line number in YAML errors when available\", async () => {\n    // Create file with error on specific line\n    // Verify error includes correct line number\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"validateFiles\", () => {\n  test(\"processes all files even when some fail\", async () => {\n    // Mix of valid and invalid files\n    // Verify all results returned\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatter\", () => {\n  test(\"formatSuccess produces expected output\", () => {\n    expect(formatSuccess(\"config.yaml\")).toBe(\"config.yaml: valid\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"formatValidationError includes line number when present\", () => {\n    const error = { message: \"bad indentation\", line: 42 };\n    expect(formatValidationError(\"config.yaml\", error))\n      .toBe(\"config.yaml (line 42): bad indentation\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### 7.3 Tests NOT to Implement\n\n| Avoided Test | Rationale |\n|--------------|-----------|\n| js-yaml parsing edge cases | Testing third-party library behavior |\n| Bun.file() error codes | Testing runtime behavior |\n| process.exit() behavior | Testing Node/Bun runtime |\n| YAML spec compliance | Testing js-yaml, not our code |\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Package.json Integration\n\nAdd script to package.json:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate\": \"bun run src/yaml-validator/index.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 Usage Examples\n\n```bash\n# Single file validation\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Multiple file validation\nbun run validate config.yaml settings.yaml data.yaml\n\n# Shell glob expansion (handled by shell)\nbun run validate *.yaml\n\n# CI/CD usage\nbun run validate config/*.yaml && echo \"All configs valid\"\n```\n\n### 8.3 No Build/Deployment Changes Required\n\n- No new dependencies to install\n- No build configuration changes\n- Bun runs TypeScript directly (no compilation step)\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | CLI Commands | N/A | Document new validate command usage |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\nSee [design-decisions.md](./design-decisions.md) for detailed decision rationale.\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice |\n|----|----------|--------|\n| D1 | YAML Parser | js-yaml (Bun built-in) |\n| D2 | Module Structure | Separate validator, formatter, types |\n| D3 | File Reading API | Bun.file() |\n| D4 | Error Line Numbers | Extract from YAMLException.mark |\n| D5 | Exit Code Priority | FILE_ERROR > VALIDATION_ERROR > SUCCESS |\n"
