        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-25\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML file syntax using Bun's built-in YAML parsing capabilities. The command accepts one or more file paths as arguments, validates each file, and reports results with appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Types have no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Validator and formatter only depend on types\n3. [T4, T5] - CLI and package.json script depend on core modules\n4. [T6] - Tests depend on all implementation components\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (validator uses types)\n- T3 -> T1 (formatter uses types)\n- T4 -> [T1, T2, T3] (CLI integrates all modules)\n- T5 -> T4 (script references entry point)\n- T6 -> [T1, T2, T3, T4] (tests verify all components)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4 -> T6\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Define TypeScript interfaces and types in types.ts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-type-definitions](design.md#31-type-definitions)\n\n    **Effort**: 1-2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] ValidationResult union type defined with success, validation_error, and file_error variants\n    - [ ] YAMLError interface defined with message, line, and column properties\n    - [ ] FileError interface defined with code and message properties\n    - [ ] ValidationSummary interface defined with total, passed, failed, and fileErrors properties\n    - [ ] ExitCode const object defined with SUCCESS (0), VALIDATION_ERROR (1), and FILE_ERROR (2)\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement core validation logic in validator.ts using js-yaml `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-validator-module](design.md#32-validator-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 4-8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] validateFile function reads file using Bun.file() API and parses with js-yaml\n    - [ ] Returns success status for syntactically valid YAML files\n    - [ ] Returns validation_error status with line number for invalid YAML syntax\n    - [ ] Returns file_error status with error code for file access failures (ENOENT, EACCES)\n    - [ ] validateFiles function processes all files without short-circuiting on errors\n    - [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement output formatting utilities in formatter.ts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-formatter-module](design.md#33-formatter-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 1-2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] formatSuccess returns \"{filePath}: valid\" format\n    - [ ] formatValidationError includes file path, line number (when available), and error message\n    - [ ] formatFileError returns \"{filePath}: {error.message}\" format\n    - [ ] formatSummary returns \"Validated N files: X passed, Y failed, Z file errors\" format\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Implement CLI entry point in index.ts with argument parsing `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-cli-entry-point](design.md#34-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 1-2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Parses file paths from process.argv.slice(2)\n    - [ ] Displays usage message and exits with code 2 when no arguments provided\n    - [ ] Outputs success messages to stdout, error messages to stderr\n    - [ ] Prints summary to stderr when multiple files validated\n    - [ ] Exits with code 0 when all files valid\n    - [ ] Exits with code 1 when any validation errors occur\n    - [ ] Exits with code 2 when any file access errors occur (takes precedence over validation errors)\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Add \"validate\" script to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-packagejson-integration](design.md#81-packagejson-integration)\n\n    **Effort**: 15 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] package.json contains \"validate\": \"bun run src/yaml-validator/index.ts\" script\n    - [ ] Command executable via \"bun run validate <file.yaml>\"\n\n### Verification\n\n- [ ] **T6**: Implement unit tests in validator.test.ts `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#72-test-cases](design.md#72-test-cases)\n\n    **Effort**: 4-8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test validateFile returns success for valid YAML\n    - [ ] Test validateFile returns validation_error with line number for invalid YAML\n    - [ ] Test validateFile returns file_error with ENOENT for non-existent files\n    - [ ] Test validateFiles processes all files even when some fail\n    - [ ] Test formatSuccess produces expected output format\n    - [ ] Test formatValidationError includes line number when present\n    - [ ] All tests pass with \"bun test\"\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Create documentation for README.md - CLI Commands `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: CLI Commands\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New CLI Commands section created in README.md\n    - [ ] Documents \"bun run validate\" command usage\n    - [ ] Includes examples for single file, multiple files, and glob patterns\n    - [ ] Documents exit codes (0, 1, 2) and their meanings\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n### REQ-001: Single File Validation\n- [ ] Given a valid file path to a syntactically correct YAML file, the command exits with code 0\n- [ ] Given a valid file path to a syntactically incorrect YAML file, the command exits with code 1\n- [ ] The file path is provided as a positional command-line argument\n\n### REQ-002: Multiple File Validation\n- [ ] Given multiple file paths, all files are validated regardless of individual failures\n- [ ] Validation continues through all files even when errors are encountered\n- [ ] Final exit code reflects the aggregate result of all validations\n\n### REQ-003: Syntax Error Reporting\n- [ ] Error messages are written to stderr (not stdout)\n- [ ] Error messages include the file path that failed\n- [ ] Error messages include the line number where the error was detected (when available from parser)\n- [ ] Error messages include a description of what syntax error was found\n- [ ] Error messages are understandable without consulting external documentation\n\n### REQ-004: Success Reporting\n- [ ] Success messages are written to stdout\n- [ ] Success messages include the file path that was validated\n- [ ] Success messages are concise (single line per file)\n\n### REQ-005: Exit Code for Validation Success\n- [ ] Exit code is 0 when all files are valid YAML\n- [ ] Exit code is 0 when a single valid file is provided\n- [ ] Exit code is 0 when multiple valid files are provided\n\n### REQ-006: Exit Code for Validation Errors\n- [ ] Exit code is 1 when any file contains invalid YAML syntax\n- [ ] Exit code is 1 regardless of how many files fail (one or multiple)\n- [ ] Exit code is 1 even if some files pass and others fail\n\n### REQ-007: Exit Code for File Access Errors\n- [ ] Exit code is 2 when a specified file does not exist\n- [ ] Exit code is 2 when a specified file cannot be read (permission denied)\n- [ ] Exit code is 2 takes precedence if both file access errors and validation errors occur\n- [ ] Error message to stderr indicates which file(s) could not be accessed\n\n### REQ-008: No New Dependencies\n- [ ] No new entries added to dependency manifest files\n- [ ] Implementation uses existing YAML parsing capabilities\n- [ ] Feature functions correctly with current project dependencies\n\n### REQ-009: Aggregate Error Summary\n- [ ] Summary indicates total number of files checked\n- [ ] Summary indicates number of files that passed\n- [ ] Summary indicates number of files that failed\n- [ ] Summary is displayed after all individual file results\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n"
