        "new_string": "## CLI Commands\n\n### YAML Validator\n\nValidate YAML file syntax from the command line.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```bash\nbun run validate <file1.yaml> [file2.yaml] ...\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Single file validation\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Multiple file validation\nbun run validate config.yaml settings.yaml data.yaml\n\n# Shell glob expansion (handled by shell)\nbun run validate *.yaml\n\n# CI/CD usage\nbun run validate config/*.yaml && echo \"All configs valid\"\n```\n\n**Exit Codes:**\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | All files are valid YAML |\n| 1 | One or more files have YAML syntax errors |\n| 2 | One or more files could not be found or read |\n\n**Output:**\n\n- Success messages are written to stdout\n- Error messages and summary are written to stderr\n- When validating multiple files, a summary is displayed after all results\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts    - Main entry point\n  utils.ts    - Utility functions\n```"
