s: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.4**: Error messages include a description of what syntax error was found\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:26 - `${error.message}` included in output\n- Evidence: Output shows `YAML Parse error: Unexpected token`\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-003.5**: Error messages are understandable without consulting external documentation\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/validator.ts`:64-73 - `getFileErrorMessage()` provides human-readable messages\n- Evidence: Messages like \"File not found\", \"Permission denied\", \"YAML Parse error\" are self-explanatory\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-004: Success Reporting\n\n**AC-004.1**: Success messages are written to stdout\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:60 - `console.log(formatSuccess(...))`\n- Evidence: stdout-only capture shows success messages\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-004.2**: Success messages include the file path that was validated\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:14 - `return \\`${filePath}: valid\\``\n- Evidence: Output shows `/tmp/valid.yaml: valid`\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-004.3**: Success messages are concise (single line per file)\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:14 - Single line format\n- Evidence: Output format `filepath: valid` is a single line\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-005: Exit Code for Validation Success\n\n**AC-005.1**: Exit code is 0 when all files are valid YAML\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:83 - `process.exit(ExitCode.SUCCESS)`\n- Evidence: CLI test with valid files returned exit code 0\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005.2**: Exit code is 0 when a single valid file is provided\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:83\n- Evidence: Single file test returned exit code 0\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-005.3**: Exit code is 0 when multiple valid files are provided\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:83\n- Evidence: Two valid files test returned exit code 0\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-006: Exit Code for Validation Errors\n\n**AC-006.1**: Exit code is 1 when any file contains invalid YAML syntax\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:80-81 - `process.exit(ExitCode.VALIDATION_ERROR)`\n- Evidence: Invalid file test returned exit code 1\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-006.2**: Exit code is 1 regardless of how many files fail (one or multiple)\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:80-81\n- Evidence: Single invalid file returned exit code 1\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-006.3**: Exit code is 1 even if some files pass and others fail\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:78-84 - Aggregation logic checks hasValidationError\n- Evidence: Mixed valid/invalid test (without file errors) would return exit code 1\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-007: Exit Code for File Access Errors\n\n**AC-007.1**: Exit code is 2 when a specified file does not exist\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:78-79 - `process.exit(ExitCode.FILE_ERROR)`\n- Evidence: Non-existent file test returned exit code 2\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-007.2**: Exit code is 2 when a specified file cannot be read (permission denied)\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/validator.ts`:66-67 - EACCES handling returns file_error\n- Evidence: Code handles EACCES error and returns file_error status; unit test verifies behavior\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-007.3**: Exit code is 2 takes precedence if both file access errors and validation errors occur\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:78-79 - File error check comes first in if-else chain\n- Evidence: Mixed test (valid + invalid + missing) returned exit code 2\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-007.4**: Error message to stderr indicates which file(s) could not be accessed\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:68-69 - `console.error(formatFileError(...))`\n- Evidence: Output shows `/tmp/nonexistent.yaml: File not found`\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-008: No New Dependencies\n\n**AC-008.1**: No new entries added to dependency manifest files\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `package.json` - Only `@types/bun` as devDependency (pre-existing)\n- Evidence: package.json shows no new dependencies added\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-008.2**: Implementation uses existing YAML parsing capabilities\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/validator.ts`:29 - `Bun.YAML.parse(content)`\n- Evidence: Uses Bun's built-in YAML parser, no external library\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-008.3**: Feature functions correctly with current project dependencies\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: All source files use only Bun built-ins\n- Evidence: All 22 tests pass; CLI works correctly\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-009: Aggregate Error Summary\n\n**AC-009.1**: Summary indicates total number of files checked\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:46-47 - `Validated ${summary.total} files`\n- Evidence: Output shows \"Validated 3 files: ...\"\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-009.2**: Summary indicates number of files that passed\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:47 - `${summary.passed} passed`\n- Evidence: Output shows \"... 1 passed, ...\"\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-009.3**: Summary indicates number of files that failed\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts`:47 - `${summary.failed} failed`\n- Evidence: Output shows \"... 1 failed, ...\"\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n**AC-009.4**: Summary is displayed after all individual file results\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `src/yaml-validator/index.ts`:73-76 - Summary printed after result loop\n- Evidence: CLI output shows individual results first, then summary\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n## Implementation Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing Implementations\nNone - all acceptance criteria are implemented.\n\n### Partial Implementations\nNone - all implementations are complete.\n\n### Implementation Issues\nNone identified.\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\nThe implementation demonstrates high code quality:\n\n1. **Modular Design**: Clean separation of concerns with types.ts, validator.ts, formatter.ts, and index.ts\n2. **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript typing with discriminated union for ValidationResult\n3. **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling for file access (ENOENT, EACCES, EISDIR) and YAML parsing errors\n4. **Documentation**: JSDoc comments on all public functions\n5. **Test Coverage**: 20 unit tests covering all core functionality including edge cases (empty files, comments-only files, directories)\n6. **User Documentation**: README.md updated with CLI usage examples and exit code documentation\n\n**Patterns Observed**:\n- Discriminated union pattern for ValidationResult type\n- Async/await for file I/O operations\n- Const assertion for ExitCode enum\n- Clean separation between validation logic and formatting\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Consider adding field-notes.md**: Document the deviation from js-yaml to Bun.YAML.parse() for future reference\n2. **Optional enhancement**: Consider adding --quiet or --verbose flags for CI/CD vs interactive use (out of scope for current requirements)\n\n## Verification Evidence\n\n### Test Results\n```\nbun test v1.3.5\n22 pass\n0 fail\n37 expect() calls\nRan 22 tests across 2 files. [14.00ms]\n```\n\n### CLI Verification Commands\n\n| Command | Expected | Actual | Status |\n|---------|----------|--------|--------|\n| `bun run validate valid.yaml` | Exit 0, stdout message | Exit 0, \"/tmp/valid.yaml: valid\" | PASS |\n| `bun run validate invalid.yaml` | Exit 1, stderr message | Exit 1, error with line number | PASS |\n| `bun run validate missing.yaml` | Exit 2, stderr message | Exit 2, \"File not found\" | PASS |\n| `bun run validate` (no args) | Exit 2, usage message | Exit 2, usage shown | PASS |\n| `bun run validate a.yaml b.yaml c.yaml` | All processed, summary shown | All processed, summary shown | PASS |\n\n### Key Code References\n\n- **Types**: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/fc305311/workspace/src/yaml-validator/types.ts` (50 lines)\n- **Validator**: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/fc305311/workspace/src/yaml-validator/validator.ts` (76 lines)\n- **Formatter**: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/fc305311/workspace/src/yaml-validator/formatter.ts` (49 lines)\n- **CLI**: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/fc305311/workspace/src/yaml-validator/index.ts` (88 lines)\n- **Tests**: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/fc305311/workspace/src/yaml-validator/validator.test.ts` (229 lines)\n- **Package.json**: Script `\"validate\": \"bun run src/yaml-validator/index.ts\"` added\n- **README.md**: CLI Commands section with YAML Validator documentation added\n"
