### 7.3 Tests NOT to Implement

| Avoided Test | Rationale |
|--------------|-----------|
| js-yaml parsing edge cases | Testing third-party library behavior |
| Bun.file() error codes | Testing runtime behavior |
| process.exit() behavior | Testing Node/Bun runtime |
| YAML spec compliance | Testing js-yaml, not our code |

## 8. Deployment Design

### 8.1 Package.json Integration

Add script to package.json:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "validate": "bun run src/yaml-validator/index.ts"
  }
}
```

### 8.2 Usage Examples

```bash
# Single file validation
bun run validate config.yaml

# Multiple file validation
bun run validate config.yaml settings.yaml data.yaml

# Shell glob expansion (handled by shell)
bun run validate *.yaml

# CI/CD usage
bun run validate config/*.yaml && echo "All configs valid"
```

### 8.3 No Build/Deployment Changes Required

- No new dependencies to install
- No build configuration changes
- Bun runs TypeScript directly (no compilation step)

## 9. Documentation Impact

| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |
|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|
| add | README.md | CLI Commands | N/A | Document new validate command usage |

## 10. Design Decisions Log

See [design-decisions.md](./design-decisions.md) for detailed decision rationale.

