# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command

**Feature ID**: yaml-validator
**Version**: 1.0.0
**Status**: Draft
**Created**: 2026-01-25

## 1. Design Overview

A CLI command that validates YAML file syntax using Bun's built-in YAML parsing capabilities. The command accepts one or more file paths as arguments, validates each file, and reports results with appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.

### High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph CLI["CLI Layer"]
        A[yaml-validator.ts<br/>Entry Point]
    end

    subgraph Core["Core Layer"]
        B[validator.ts<br/>Validation Logic]
        C[formatter.ts<br/>Output Formatting]
    end

    subgraph External["External"]
        D[(File System)]
        E[js-yaml<br/>Bun Built-in]
    end

    A --> B
    A --> C
    B --> D
    B --> E
    C --> F[stdout/stderr]
```

## 2. Architecture

### 2.1 Component Structure

The implementation follows the existing project structure with modular separation of concerns:

```
src/
  yaml-validator/
    index.ts        # CLI entry point
    validator.ts    # Core validation logic
    formatter.ts    # Output formatting utilities
    types.ts        # TypeScript type definitions
    validator.test.ts  # Unit tests
```

### 2.2 Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant CLI as yaml-validator/index.ts
    participant Val as validator.ts
    participant Fmt as formatter.ts
    participant FS as File System
    participant YAML as js-yaml

    User->>CLI: bun run validate file1.yaml file2.yaml
    CLI->>CLI: Parse argv for file paths

    loop For each file path
        CLI->>Val: validateFile(path)
        Val->>FS: Bun.file(path).text()
        alt File not found/readable
            FS-->>Val: Error
            Val-->>CLI: FileAccessError
        else File readable
            FS-->>Val: content
            Val->>YAML: parse(content)
            alt Parse error
                YAML-->>Val: YAMLException
                Val-->>CLI: ValidationError
            else Parse success
                YAML-->>Val: parsed object
                Val-->>CLI: ValidationSuccess
            end
        end
        CLI->>Fmt: formatResult(result)
        Fmt-->>CLI: formatted message
        CLI->>User: stdout/stderr output
    end

    CLI->>Fmt: formatSummary(results)
    Fmt-->>CLI: summary message
    CLI->>User: Summary to stderr
    CLI->>User: Exit with code (0/1/2)
```

## 3. Detailed Design

### 3.1 Type Definitions

```typescript
// types.ts

/** Result of validating a single file */
export type ValidationResult =
  | { status: 'success'; filePath: string }
  | { status: 'validation_error'; filePath: string; error: YAMLError }
  | { status: 'file_error'; filePath: string; error: FileError };

/** YAML parsing error details */
export interface YAMLError {
  message: string;
  line?: number;
  column?: number;
}

/** File access error details */
export interface FileError {
  code: string;  // 'ENOENT', 'EACCES', etc.
  message: string;
}

/** Aggregate results for multiple files */
export interface ValidationSummary {
  total: number;
  passed: number;
  failed: number;
  fileErrors: number;
}

/** Exit codes */
export const ExitCode = {
  SUCCESS: 0,
  VALIDATION_ERROR: 1,
  FILE_ERROR: 2,
} as const;

export type ExitCode = typeof ExitCode[keyof typeof ExitCode];
```

### 3.2 Validator Module

