### 3.4 CLI Entry Point

```typescript
// index.ts

import { validateFiles } from "./validator";
import { formatSuccess, formatValidationError, formatFileError, formatSummary } from "./formatter";
import { ExitCode } from "./types";

async function main(): Promise<never> {
  const filePaths = process.argv.slice(2);

  if (filePaths.length === 0) {
    console.error("Usage: bun run validate <file1.yaml> [file2.yaml] ...");
    process.exit(ExitCode.FILE_ERROR);
  }

  const results = await validateFiles(filePaths);

  let hasFileError = false;
  let hasValidationError = false;

  for (const result of results) {
    switch (result.status) {
      case 'success':
        console.log(formatSuccess(result.filePath));
        break;
      case 'validation_error':
        console.error(formatValidationError(result.filePath, result.error));
        hasValidationError = true;
        break;
      case 'file_error':
        console.error(formatFileError(result.filePath, result.error));
        hasFileError = true;
        break;
    }
  }

  // Print summary if multiple files
  if (results.length > 1) {
    const summary = calculateSummary(results);
    console.error(formatSummary(summary));
  }

  // Exit code priority: file error > validation error > success
  if (hasFileError) {
    process.exit(ExitCode.FILE_ERROR);
  } else if (hasValidationError) {
    process.exit(ExitCode.VALIDATION_ERROR);
  } else {
    process.exit(ExitCode.SUCCESS);
  }
}

main();
```

### 3.5 Data Model

No persistent data storage. The command processes files and produces output in a single invocation.

**In-Memory Data Structures:**

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Input
        A[string[]: filePaths]
    end

    subgraph Processing
        B[ValidationResult[]]
    end

    subgraph Output
        C[stdout: success messages]
        D[stderr: error messages + summary]
        E[exit code: 0/1/2]
    end

    A --> B
    B --> C
    B --> D
    B --> E
```

## 4. Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology | Justification |
|-------|------------|---------------|
| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |
| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |
| YAML Parser | js-yaml (Bun built-in) | No new dependencies required |
| File I/O | Bun.file() API | Native Bun file handling |
| Testing | bun:test | Existing project test framework |

**Critical Constraint**: No new dependencies. The implementation uses only:
- Bun runtime built-ins
- @types/bun (existing devDependency)

## 5. Implementation Plan

| Task | Component | Description | Effort |
|------|-----------|-------------|--------|
| T1 | types.ts | Define TypeScript interfaces and types | Small |
| T2 | validator.ts | Core validation logic using js-yaml | Medium |
| T3 | formatter.ts | Output formatting utilities | Small |
| T4 | index.ts | CLI entry point with argument parsing | Small |
| T5 | package.json | Add "validate" script | Trivial |
| T6 | validator.test.ts | Unit tests for validator and formatter | Medium |

**Estimated Total Effort**: Small-Medium (single session)

## 6. Implementation DAG

**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):

1. [T1] - Types have no dependencies
2. [T2, T3] - Validator and formatter only depend on types
3. [T4, T5] - CLI and package.json script depend on core modules
4. [T6] - Tests depend on all implementation components

**Dependencies**:

- T2 -> T1 (validator uses types)
- T3 -> T1 (formatter uses types)
- T4 -> [T1, T2, T3] (CLI integrates all modules)
- T5 -> T4 (script references entry point)
- T6 -> [T1, T2, T3, T4] (tests verify all components)

**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4 -> T6

## 7. Testing Strategy

### 7.1 Test Value Assessment

| Test Type | Value | Rationale |
|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Valid YAML parsing | HIGH | Core app functionality |
| Invalid YAML detection | HIGH | Core app functionality |
| File not found handling | HIGH | Exit code correctness for CI/CD |
| Permission denied handling | MEDIUM | Error handling path |
| Exit code verification | HIGH | CI/CD integration correctness |
| Output stream routing | HIGH | stdout vs stderr correctness |
| Summary formatting | LOW | Cosmetic, not critical path |

