        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-25\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nA command-line utility for validating YAML file syntax, implemented in pure TypeScript without additional npm dependencies. The validator provides clear success/failure feedback with error details including line numbers.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        A[yaml-validate.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Validation Core\"]\n        B[yaml-validator.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IO[\"I/O Sources\"]\n        C[File System]\n        D[stdin]\n    end\n\n    C --> A\n    D --> A\n    A --> B\n    B --> E[Validation Result]\n    E --> F[stdout/stderr]\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Overview\n\n| Component | Responsibility | Location |\n|-----------|---------------|----------|\n| CLI Entry Point | Parse args, read input, orchestrate flow, output results | `src/yaml-validate.ts` |\n| YAML Validator | Core validation logic, error detection, result formatting | `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n| Tests | Unit tests for validator functions | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` |\n\n### 2.2 Component Interaction\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as yaml-validate.ts\n    participant Validator as yaml-validator.ts\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant Stdin as stdin\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run yaml-validate.ts [file|--help]\n\n    alt --help flag\n        CLI->>User: Display usage info\n    else file path provided\n        CLI->>FS: Read file content\n        FS-->>CLI: YAML content\n    else no args (stdin)\n        CLI->>Stdin: Read piped content\n        Stdin-->>CLI: YAML content\n    end\n\n    CLI->>Validator: validateYaml(content)\n    Validator-->>CLI: ValidationResult\n\n    alt valid\n        CLI->>User: \"Valid YAML\" (exit 0)\n    else invalid\n        CLI->>User: Error details (exit 1)\n    end\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Module: yaml-validator.ts\n\nCore validation module implementing YAML syntax checking.\n\n#### Interfaces\n\n```typescript\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\ninterface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column?: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n```\n\n#### Functions\n\n| Function | Signature | Purpose |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| `validateYaml` | `(content: string) => ValidationResult` | Main validation entry point |\n| `checkIndentation` | `(lines: string[]) => ValidationError[]` | Validate consistent indentation |\n| `checkQuotes` | `(lines: string[]) => ValidationError[]` | Check for unclosed quotes |\n| `checkBrackets` | `(lines: string[]) => ValidationError[]` | Validate bracket/brace matching |\n| `checkKeyValueSyntax` | `(lines: string[]) => ValidationError[]` | Validate key: value format |\n| `checkMultiDocument` | `(lines: string[]) => ValidationError[]` | Validate document separators |\n\n#### Validation Rules\n\n| Rule | Description | Error Message Example |\n|------|-------------|----------------------|\n| Indentation | Spaces only, consistent width | \"Inconsistent indentation at line 5\" |\n| Quotes | Matching single/double quotes | \"Unclosed quote at line 3\" |\n| Brackets | Matching [], {} pairs | \"Unclosed bracket '[' at line 7\" |\n| Key-Value | Colon followed by space or newline | \"Invalid key-value syntax at line 2\" |\n| Tabs | No tab characters | \"Tab character found at line 4\" |\n\n### 3.2 Module: yaml-validate.ts\n\nCLI entry point handling argument parsing and I/O.\n\n#### Flow\n\n1. Parse command-line arguments\n2. Handle --help/-h flag\n3. Determine input source (file or stdin)\n4. Read content\n5. Call validator\n6. Output result\n7. Exit with appropriate code\n\n#### Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | Valid YAML |\n| 1 | Invalid YAML (syntax error) |\n| 2 | File not found |\n| 3 | Read error |\n\n#### CLI Interface\n\n```\nUsage: bun run src/yaml-validate.ts [options] [file]\n\nArguments:\n  file          Path to YAML file to validate\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Show this help message\n\nExamples:\n  bun run src/yaml-validate.ts config.yaml\n  cat config.yaml | bun run src/yaml-validate.ts\n  echo \"key: value\" | bun run src/yaml-validate.ts\n```\n\n### 3.3 Input Handling\n\n| Source | Detection | Method |\n|--------|-----------|--------|\n| File | `process.argv[2]` exists and not a flag | `Bun.file(path).text()` |\n| stdin | No file argument provided | `await Bun.stdin.text()` |\n\n### 3.4 Edge Cases\n\n| Case | Handling |\n|------|----------|\n| Empty file | Valid (empty document per BR-002) |\n| Comments only | Valid (per BR-003) |\n| Multi-document | Validate all documents (per BR-004) |\n| Binary file | Report error (not valid YAML) |\n| Very large file | Process normally (Bun handles streaming) |\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Project standard; required by constraints |\n| Language | TypeScript | Project standard; type safety |\n| Testing | bun:test | Project standard; no additional deps |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() | Built-in, performant |\n| stdin | Bun.stdin | Built-in stdin handling |\n\n### Dependencies\n\n**No new dependencies required.** Implementation uses:\n- Bun runtime APIs (file, stdin)\n- Standard TypeScript/JavaScript (string manipulation, regex)\n- bun:test for testing (already available)\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| Phase | Task | Description | Effort |\n|-------|------|-------------|--------|\n| T1 | Create yaml-validator.ts | Core validation logic with all rule checks | Medium |\n| T2 | Create yaml-validate.ts | CLI entry point with arg parsing and I/O | Small |\n| T3 | Create yaml-validator.test.ts | Unit tests for validator functions | Medium |\n| T4 | Add npm script | Add \"validate\" script to package.json | Trivial |\n| T5 | Manual testing | Test with real YAML files | Small |\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core validator has no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend only on T1\n3. [T4, T5] - Both depend on T2\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports validator functions)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import validator functions)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references CLI entry point)\n- T5 -> T2 (Sequential: Manual testing requires working CLI)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T5\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Approach\n\nFocus on testing application-specific validation logic.\n\n| Test Category | Purpose | Value |\n|---------------|---------|-------|\n| Valid YAML cases | Confirm valid files pass | HIGH - Core requirement |\n| Invalid YAML cases | Confirm errors detected with line numbers | HIGH - Core requirement |\n| Edge cases | Empty, comments-only, multi-doc | MEDIUM - Business rules |\n| Error messages | Verify actionable error text | MEDIUM - Usability |\n\n### 7.2 Test Cases\n\n```typescript\n// yaml-validator.test.ts\n\ndescribe(\"validateYaml\", () => {\n  // Valid cases\n  test(\"accepts valid key-value YAML\");\n  test(\"accepts valid nested YAML\");\n  test(\"accepts empty content\");\n  test(\"accepts comments-only content\");\n  test(\"accepts multi-document YAML\");\n\n  // Invalid cases\n  test(\"rejects unclosed quotes\");\n  test(\"rejects tab indentation\");\n  test(\"rejects inconsistent indentation\");\n  test(\"rejects unclosed brackets\");\n  test(\"rejects invalid key-value syntax\");\n\n  // Error details\n  test(\"reports correct line number for error\");\n  test(\"provides descriptive error message\");\n});\n```\n\n### 7.3 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Include | Rationale |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Validation logic tests | Core business logic |\n| Error reporting tests | Application requirement |\n| Edge case tests | Business rules BR-002, BR-003, BR-004 |\n\n| Exclude | Rationale |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Bun.file() behavior | Tests Bun runtime, not our code |\n| String.split() behavior | Tests JavaScript, not our code |\n| process.argv parsing | Minimal logic, integration tested |\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Integration\n\nNo deployment infrastructure changes required. Feature adds:\n- New TypeScript files in `src/`\n- New npm script in `package.json`\n\n### 8.2 Usage\n\n```bash\n# Direct execution\nbun run src/yaml-validate.ts config.yaml\n\n# Via npm script (after adding to package.json)\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Stdin\ncat config.yaml | bun run src/yaml-validate.ts\n```\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | README.md | Scripts | N/A | Add validate script documentation |\n| edit | README.md | Structure | N/A | Add new files to structure diagram |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Pure TypeScript syntax validator | No new deps constraint; full parser too complex |\n| D2 | File organization | Separate validator module | Testability; separation of concerns |\n| D3 | Exit codes | 0=valid, 1=invalid, 2=not found, 3=read error | Standard CLI conventions; scriptability |\n| D4 | Error format | \"Error at line N: description\" | Matches requirement for line numbers |\n| D5 | stdin detection | Check if file arg provided | Simple, follows existing pattern |\n\n## Appendix: Validation Limitations\n\nThe pure TypeScript validator focuses on common syntax errors. It does not implement a full YAML 1.2 parser. Known limitations:\n\n| Limitation | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------------|--------|------------|\n| Complex flow scalars | May not validate all edge cases | Focus on common patterns |\n| Anchors/aliases | Basic syntax check only | Validates syntax, not references |\n| Custom tags | Not validated | Out of scope for syntax check |\n\nThese limitations are acceptable for the MVP given the constraint of no additional dependencies.\n"
      },
      "source": "assistant"
    },
