        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-25\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line utility for validating YAML file syntax, implemented in pure TypeScript without additional npm dependencies. The validator provides clear success/failure feedback with error details including line numbers. Supports both file path arguments and stdin input.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core validator has no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend only on T1\n3. [T4, T5] - Both depend on T2\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports validator functions)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import validator functions)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references CLI entry point)\n- T5 -> T2 (Sequential: Manual testing requires working CLI)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T5\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Phase 1: Core Validation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create yaml-validator.ts with core validation logic including indentation, quote, bracket, key-value syntax, and multi-document checks `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-module-yaml-validatorts](design.md#31-module-yaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] ValidationResult and ValidationError interfaces defined per design spec\n    - [ ] validateYaml() function returns valid:true for correct YAML syntax\n    - [ ] checkIndentation() detects inconsistent spacing and tab characters\n    - [ ] checkQuotes() detects unclosed single and double quotes\n    - [ ] checkBrackets() detects unclosed [] and {} pairs\n    - [ ] checkKeyValueSyntax() validates colon followed by space or newline\n    - [ ] checkMultiDocument() validates document separators (---)\n    - [ ] All errors include line number and descriptive message\n    - [ ] Empty content returns valid:true (BR-002)\n    - [ ] Comments-only content returns valid:true (BR-003)\n\n### Phase 2: CLI and Tests\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Create yaml-validate.ts CLI entry point with argument parsing, file/stdin input handling, and formatted output `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-module-yaml-validatets](design.md#32-module-yaml-validatets)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Parses command-line arguments for file path and --help/-h flag\n    - [ ] Displays usage information when --help or -h flag provided\n    - [ ] Reads file content using Bun.file() when path argument provided\n    - [ ] Reads stdin content using Bun.stdin when no file argument\n    - [ ] Outputs \"Valid YAML\" message for valid content\n    - [ ] Outputs error details with line numbers for invalid content\n    - [ ] Exit code 0 for valid YAML\n    - [ ] Exit code 1 for invalid YAML syntax\n    - [ ] Exit code 2 for file not found\n    - [ ] Exit code 3 for read errors\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Create yaml-validator.test.ts with comprehensive unit tests for all validation functions `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test accepts valid key-value YAML\n    - [ ] Test accepts valid nested YAML\n    - [ ] Test accepts empty content\n    - [ ] Test accepts comments-only content\n    - [ ] Test accepts multi-document YAML\n    - [ ] Test rejects unclosed quotes\n    - [ ] Test rejects tab indentation\n    - [ ] Test rejects inconsistent indentation\n    - [ ] Test rejects unclosed brackets\n    - [ ] Test rejects invalid key-value syntax\n    - [ ] Test verifies correct line number in error\n    - [ ] Test verifies descriptive error messages\n    - [ ] All tests pass with bun test\n\n### Phase 3: Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Add validate script to package.json for convenient command execution `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#5-implementation-plan](design.md#5-implementation-plan)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] package.json contains \"validate\" script\n    - [ ] Script executes src/yaml-validate.ts\n    - [ ] Command works via `bun run validate <file>`\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Manual testing with real YAML files covering valid, invalid, and edge cases `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#5-implementation-plan](design.md#5-implementation-plan)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Validate known-good YAML file returns success\n    - [ ] Validate known-bad YAML file returns error with line number\n    - [ ] Stdin piping works correctly\n    - [ ] Help flag displays usage information\n    - [ ] File not found returns appropriate error\n    - [ ] Performance acceptable for files under 1MB (<500ms)\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Scripts section documents the validate command\n    - [ ] Usage examples included for file and stdin modes\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update README.md - Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Structure section includes yaml-validate.ts\n    - [ ] Structure section includes yaml-validator.ts\n    - [ ] Structure section includes yaml-validator.test.ts\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] FR-001: File path validation - accepts file path as command-line argument and validates YAML content\n- [ ] FR-002: Standard input validation - accepts YAML content from stdin when no file path provided\n- [ ] FR-003: Success output - displays \"Valid YAML\" message and returns exit code 0 for valid content\n- [ ] FR-004: Error output with details - displays line number and error description for invalid content with non-zero exit\n- [ ] FR-005: File not found handling - displays \"File not found\" error for missing files\n- [ ] FR-006: Help information - displays usage info when invoked with --help or -h\n- [ ] BR-001: No new npm dependencies added\n- [ ] BR-002: Empty files considered valid\n- [ ] BR-003: Comments-only files considered valid\n- [ ] BR-004: Multi-document YAML files validated correctly\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n"
